{"id":"H1724","lemma":"דָּהַם","transliteration":"daham","sayIt":"da-ham","language":"Hebrew","partOfSpeech":"verb","gloss":"to astonish","meaning":"1) to astonish, astound\n1a) (Niphal) astounded (participle)","glosses":["taken by surprise"],"count":1,"occurrences":[{"chapterId":"jer-14","v":9,"renderings":{"bsb":"taken by surprise","kjv":"astonied"}}],"elsewhere":[{"ref":"Jeremiah 14:9","note":"Why should you be like a scared man, as a mighty man who can’t save? Yet you, Yahweh, are in the middle of us, and we are called by your name. Don’t leave us.","source":"web"}],"related":[],"sources":["STEPBible TBESH/TBESG lexicon (CC BY 4.0)","STEPBible TAHOT/TAGNT tagged text (CC BY 4.0)"]}